# Allow-list: everything is excluded, then the runtime files are added back (vsce lets a "!" rule win over
# every exclusion). Keep it in step with the file check in scripts/package.ps1 (Assert-VsixContents) and with
# docs/en/packaging.md.
# The screenshots of the README (media/workbench-*.png) are left out on purpose: vsce rewrites the relative image
# and link paths of README.md and CHANGELOG.md to the GitHub URLs of package.json "repository".
# README.md is not listed: scripts/package.ps1 passes a README derived from it with --readme-path, and vsce
# adds that file as extension/readme.md itself.
**
!dist/extension.js
!dist/sql-wasm.wasm
!dist/grid-client.js
!dist/report-client.js
!dist/plan-client.js
!media/icon.png
!media/logo.png
!media/aantje-activity.svg
!media/aantje-icons.woff
!package.json
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
!docs/en/**
# The native DuckDB bindings are the only runtime dependency that is not bundled. npm installs only the
# binding of the platform it runs on, so each platform-specific VSIX gets exactly one.
!node_modules/@duckdb/node-bindings*/**
# Output of the extension-host tests (npm run test:integration). "**" leaves both out already; this says so.
.vscode-test/**
out/**
test/.cache/**
